From d730e7745b15d738fc9cc18daaff36a995c5f0a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: newjordan <newjordan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 13:49:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: add GGML_TYPE_IQ3_A770 codebook-free 3-bit quant (CPU
 oracle)

IQ3_A770 is an A770-oriented 3-bit MoE expert quant: same qs/hmask bit
packing as Q3_K (direct unpack, no codebook/grid) but 8 sub-blocks of 32 with
4-bit signed scales -> 102 bytes/superblock = 3.1875 bpw, symmetric
(x = d*sc*(q-4)). Codebook-free so the SYCL expert GEMV (0006/0007) can read
the packed form directly.

Adds: block_iq3_a770 + static_assert; GGML_TYPE_IQ3_A770 (42) and
GGML_FTYPE_MOSTLY_IQ3_A770; CPU ref quantize/dequantize (imatrix-aware) and
quantize_iq3_a770; ggml_vec_dot_iq3_a770_q8_K (generic) + type_traits +
type_traits_cpu (vec_dot_type Q8_K); ggml_quantize_chunk, ftype map,
validate_row_data; arch-fallback alias; test-backend-ops type lists.

Usable today via: llama-quantize --tensor-type ffn_{gate,up,down}_exps=iq3_a770
on a q6_k base (Policy C). A dedicated LLAMA_FTYPE + llama_tensor_get_type policy
is deferred to a follow-up. Validated by tests/iq3_a770_oracle_check.c:
vec_dot == dequantize-then-dot (rel diff ~1e-7), round-trip NRMSE 0.142.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
